The growing adoption of the QUIC (Quick UDP Internet Connections) protocol is not matched by current measurement and benchmarking tools that can emulate QUIC traffic. Software-based solutions are constrained by CPU bottlenecks. Meanwhile, Tofino-based traffic generators do not support QUIC. We designed QU4C (QUIC traffic P4-based reproduCer), the first strategy to rely on programmable ASICs to reproduce and scale QUIC traffic at high throughput. QU4C addresses challenges such as limited ASIC memory resources and encryption constraints, enabling QUIC traffic to reach 46.6 Gbps while preserving the post-handshake flow context.